 "title": "Australia's Forgotten Air Force",
 "cat": "history",
 "emoji": "✈️",
 "sentences": [
  "Australia once had a temporary stop-gap air force.",
  "The Australian Air Corps existed between two major eras.",
  "It operated between the disbandment of the Australian Flying Corps and the Royal Australian Air Force.",
  "Major William Anderson commanded this group of former pilots.",
  "They maintained the Central Flying School at Point Cook.",
  "This team set an altitude record and flew non-stop between Sydney and Melbourne.",
  "They even pioneered early aviation medicine."
